      "content": "The 2022 F-150 has a complex hydraulic system, and the pressure spikes you're seeing could be indicative of several issues. A faulty or faulty-wiring solenoid valve in the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) could be causing the spikes, as it controls the hydraulic pressures in the transmission and traction control systems. Another possibility is a dirty or faulty park-erase sensor, which can cause fluctuations in the hydraulic circuit.",
